<div class="box-exercise"><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Book:_General_Chemistry:_Principles_Patterns_and_Applications_(Averill)/03:_Chemical_Reactions/3.02:_Determining_Empirical_and_Molecular_Formulas" class="mt-section"><span id="Exercise_.5C(.5CPageIndex.7B1.7D.5C)"></span><h5 class="box-legend lt-chem-36984 editable"><span class="lt-icon-default">Exercise \(\PageIndex{1}\)</span></h5>

<p class="para lt-chem-36984" id="av_1.0-ch07_s02_s01_p08">Calculate the mass percentage of each element in aluminum oxide (Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>). Then calculate the mass of aluminum in a 3.62 g sample of pure aluminum oxide.</p>

<dl>
    <dt><strong class="emphasis bold">Answer</strong></dt>
    <dd>
    <p class="lt-chem-36984">52.93% aluminum; 47.08% oxygen; 1.92 g Al</p>
    </dd>
</dl>
</div></div>


